  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'An electromagnet is a temporary magnet created by the flow of electric
    current. It is usually made by wrapping a coil of insulated copper wire around
    an iron core.


    When the switch is turned on, electric current flows through
    the coil and produces a magnetic field around it. The iron core strengthens this
    magnetic field and becomes magnetic, allowing the electromagnet to attract iron
    objects such as paper clips.


    When the switch is turned off, the current
    stops and the magnetic effect greatly reduces or disappears.


    The strength
    of an electromagnet can be increased by increasing the number of turns in the
    coil, increasing the electric current, or using a suitable iron core.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
